8. WHY THIS IS CERTIFIABLE

ISO 26262 ASIL-D requires:

Requirement How this architecture satisfies it
Deterministic behavior FSM + ROM-burned actions; no sampling anywhere
Bounded execution time AET = 800 cycles; every plan budget published
Traceable decisions Every action traces to a tile, a triage decision, a named signer
Safe state on failure ESCALATE policy: every safety-critical plan has a fallback
No silent failure 0x-AMBIG and 0x-WCET-EXCEEDED are first-class outputs
Verifiable behavior set B is finite, enumerated, exhaustively checked pre-deployment

The ESCALATE policy is what makes the fourth row true. Without it, a refusal would be a null state — and a null state is not a safe state.

---

9. THE VERIFIABLE AGENCY THEOREM, INSTANTIATED

Given:

· (i) a finite action library A = {A_COAST, A_BRAKE_LIGHT, A_BRAKE_MEDIUM, A_BRAKE_HARD, A_ALERT_DRIVER, A_HANDOFF}
· (ii) a finite plan library P = {PLAN_CRUISE_MAINTAIN, PLAN_FOLLOW_ADAPT, PLAN_EMERGENCY_STOP}
· (iii) an FSM with bounded transition function and bounded AET (800 cycles)
· (iv) formal preconditions and postconditions for every action

Then: the complete behavior set B = {all action sequences the agent can produce} is finite, enumerable, and exhaustively verifiable before deployment.

For this concrete case, |B| is on the order of 10³ sequences. All of them are checked before silicon.

---

10. RESIDUALS

Named, not hidden.

# Residual Status
R1 Silicon validation. Cycle counts are architectural constants. FPGA → ASIC path exists. Unbuilt. Declared
R2 Sensor trust. The BWS and DMS inputs are assumed correct. Their failure modes are a separate safety case. Out of scope
R3 Driver response time. The 0.4 s assumed in the ESCALATE path is a declared constant. Real driver response varies. Declared
R4 Cross-plan interference. This case models one plan at a time. Multi-plan scheduling is a separate problem. Out of scope
R5 Predicate coverage. Three predicates cover the three known hazard classes. A fourth may exist. Open
R6 Window length. W = 8 is a declared constant. Its sufficiency is a domain question. Declared

A standard that names its residuals is one that can be trusted.

